<!DOCTYPE concept PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA 1.3 Concept//EN" "concept.dtd">
<concept base="Top" id="t00160">
	<title>Other view modes</title>
	<conbody>
		<section id="e00832">
			<title id="e00833">Master warning mode </title>
			<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e00834">
				<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
					<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
					<tbody>
						<row rowsep="1">
							<entry colname="col1">
								<fig id="e00835">
									<image href="images/N_CT25Z021.jpg" scale="95" align="center" placement="break"/>
								</fig>
							</entry>
							<entry colname="col2"/>
						</row>
					</tbody>
				</tgroup>
			</table>
			<p>This mode informs you of the following situations:</p>
			<indexterm>LCD display modes</indexterm>
			<indexterm>master warning mode</indexterm>
			<ul id="e00836">
				<li>
					<p>Driver assistance system malfunction, limitation, or a radar or camera interference</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>LED headlamp malfunction</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>Lamp malfunction</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p>TPMS (Tire Pressure Monitoring System) failure, low tire pressure, and so on.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>The Master Warning icon (<image href="images/WKIA_007.jpg" scale="15" align="left" placement="inline"/>) will appear. If the warning situation resolves, the master warning light will turn off and the Master Warning icon will disappear.</p>
		</section>
	</conbody>
	<related-links>
		<linkpool>
			<link format="dita" href="t00156.dita#t00156" role="parent" scope="local" type="concept">
				<linktext>LCD display modes </linktext>
			</link>
		</linkpool>
	</related-links>
</concept>